antly for the Vice President for a period of at least one\nyear subsequent to January 20, 2001, in the implementation of Public Law\n93–346, as amended, or in military units and support facilities to which\nsection 1 of Executive Order 12793 of March 20, 1992, as amended, refers’’\nimmediately preceding the period;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 12579 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 1(b)","sha256":"4a783e7a5b00b9fd4ee8db2b8c13b5627b0df63f71ff06a8a52d610085491c4f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-03-14/pdf/05-5097.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13373#sec1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) in section 2, by striking ‘‘Military Assistant to the Vice President’’\nand inserting in lieu thereof ‘‘Vice President’s designee (with the concurrence\nof the Director of the White House Military Office in the case of personnel\nin military units or support facilities to which section 1 of Executive Order\n12793, as amended, refers)’’;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 12579 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 1(c)","sha256":"4a783e7a5b00b9fd4ee8db2b8c13b5627b0df63f71ff06a8a52d610085491c4f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-03-14/pdf/05-5097.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13373#sec1(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) in section 2, by inserting ‘‘and, in the case of members of the commis-\nsioned corps of the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration or\nthe commissioned corps of the Public Health Service so assigned, by the\nSecretary of Commerce or the Secretary of Health and Human Services,\nrespectively’’ immediately preceding the period;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 12579 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 1(d)","sha256":"4a783e7a5b00b9fd4ee8db2b8c13b5627b0df63f71ff06a8a52d610085491c4f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-03-14/pdf/05-5097.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13373#sec1(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(e) in section 5, by adding at the end of the section ‘‘No award shall\nbe made to an individual under this Order based on a period of service\nwith respect to which, in whole or in part, the individual was awarded\nthe Presidential Service Badge.’’;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 12579 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 1(e)","sha256":"4a783e7a5b00b9fd4ee8db2b8c13b5627b0df63f71ff06a8a52d610085491c4f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-03-14/pdf/05-5097.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13373#sec1(e)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(f) in section 6, by striking ‘‘and Coast Guard,’’ and inserting in lieu\nthereof ‘‘Coast Guard, commissioned corps of the National Oceanic and\nAtmospheric Administration, and commissioned corps of the Public Health\nService,’’;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 12579 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 1(f)","sha256":"4a783e7a5b00b9fd4ee8db2b8c13b5627b0df63f71ff06a8a52d610085491c4f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-03-14/pdf/05-5097.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13373#sec1(f)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(g) in section 6, by inserting ‘‘, or who has been assigned to perform\nduties predominantly for the Vice President, in the implementation of Public\nLaw 93–346, as amended, or in military units and support facilities to\nwhich section 1 of Executive Order 12793, as amended, refers,’’ after ‘‘Office\nof the Vice President’’;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"70 FR 12579 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 1(g)","sha256":"4a783e7a5b00b9fd4ee8db2b8c13b5627b0df63f71ff06a8a52d610085491c4f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-03-14/pdf/05-5097.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13373#sec1(g)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(h) in 